[severity:It bothers me. A fix would be nice]
I've been experiencing an issue with Razor Pages formatting in both Visual Studio and Visual Studio Code. Erroneous tabs get inserted on format. The offending Razor code is:

```
@page
@using System.Globalization
@model IndexModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Home page";
}

&lt;div class="col col-2"&gt;
    &lt;partial name="_StatCounterCard" model='@new StatCounterCardModel
        {
            Title = "Last Date",
            Subtitle = "Last date subtitle",
            IsPlaceholderLoading = false,
            StaticValue = (Model.LatestDate == null || Model.LatestDate == DateTime.MinValue)
            ? null
            : Model.LatestDate?. ToString("d", CultureInfo.CurrentCulture)
        }' /&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

@section scripts {
    &lt;script&gt;
        $(document).ready(function () {
            const config = {
                numbers: [],
                strings: []
            };

@foreach (var num in Model.Q.Numbers)
        {
            @:config.numbers.push(@num);
        }

@foreach (var str in Model.Q.Strings)
        {
            @:config.strings.push("@str");
        }
        })
    &lt;/script&gt;
}
```

To demonstrate the issue, after a couple formats with Shift+Alt+F:

```
@page
@using System.Globalization
@model IndexModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Home page";
}

&lt;div class="col col-2"&gt;
    &lt;partial name="_StatCounterCard" model='@new StatCounterCardModel
             {
                 Title = "Last Date",
                 Subtitle = "Last date subtitle",
                 IsPlaceholderLoading = false,
                 StaticValue = (Model.LatestDate == null || Model.LatestDate == DateTime.MinValue)
                            ? null
                            : Model.LatestDate?. ToString("d", CultureInfo.CurrentCulture)
             }' /&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

@section scripts {
    &lt;script&gt;
        $(document).ready(function() {
            const config = {
                numbers: [],
                strings: []
            };

@foreach (var num in Model.Q.Numbers)
                {
                    @:config.numbers.push(@num);
            }

@foreach (var str in Model.Q.Strings)
                {
                    @:config.strings.push("@str");
            }
                                        })
    &lt;/script&gt;
}
```

As you can see, both the partial multiline ternary operator and JavaScript `@foreach` lines experience getting extra indentation on each format, sending them on a journey across the screen. Additionally, I get the warning `(JS) Expression expected.` at the end of the `$(document).ready(` closing '}' bracket.

I have created a repository ready to use to demonstrate these issues at https://github.com/canyon-online/FormattingTests. My code cleanup profile includes: Remove unused variables, Remove unnecessary casts, Remove unused suppressions, and Apply namespace preferences. My VS version is 18.9.0 August 2026 Feature Update.

